{
  "_comment": "The wire contract of split jobs that arrive over HTTP. A POST writes one source message: the key and the value are the request id (UTF-8) and the raw request body, the partition is left to the key partitioner (-1), and the headers are source_message_header_order, each value UTF-8 text. A status record has the request id as its key (UTF-8), the one header dk-status-version = 1, and a value of compact JSON with sorted keys, raw UTF-8. In the input of a status case, updated_at is the text the value carries, and result is the JSON text of the result. A status map keeps one record per request id: for another job the lower source offset wins, for the same job the state rank that is equal or higher wins; an end state older than retention_seconds at now is not stored and removes the stored entry of its own job, and a lower-rank record of that job read after it is not stored. Encoding of bytes in this file: a JSON string is its UTF-8 bytes, {\"base64\": \"...\"} is the decoded bytes, null is no value.",
